From 5b5f3c7507ef4f9cab4acdf0f03903c2d19ff62a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: riceharvest <myappleiddarimaan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:50:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/15] [MoE] Int4 GEMV for decode-sized grouped GEMMs

At decode each routed expert sees one row, and the int4 grouped GEMM's fixed
cost per call dominates: 8 experts of Qwen3.6-35B-A3B are 13 MB of weights
(~21 us at full bandwidth on a B70), but a gate_up call takes ~56 us and a
down call ~34 us.

Add _xpu_C.moe_int4_gemv for the int4 layout cutlass_grouped_gemm_interface
already uses (int8-packed signed 4-bit weights [E, N, K/2], per-group scales
[E, N, K/G]) and route int4 calls with at most 8 rows to it from
XpuFusedMoe. Larger calls (prefill, MTP verify, batched decode) keep the
grouped GEMM. VLLM_XPU_FUSED_MOE_INT4_GEMV=0 disables the new path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: riceharvest <myappleiddarimaan@gmail.com>

